 ## Overview
-This method renders arbitrary slicing planes through a volume by interpolating between two adjacent object-aligned texture slices using multi-texturing hardware. It solves the problem of rendering non-axis-aligned cross-sections without requiring 3D texture storage or complex ray-casting, by decomposing the arbitrary slice into polygon strips that span only two 2D textures. It sets itself apart from single-texture approaches by reducing the polygon count by half, though it is constrained by memory bandwidth limitations [S1].
