 ## Background
-This method was developed for interactive volume rendering on standard PC graphics hardware in the early 2000s. It was implemented on Windows NT with an NVIDIA GeForce 256 processor. The technique leverages the multi-texturing capabilities of early GPUs to perform linear interpolation between 2D texture slices, enabling efficient multi-planar reformatting (MPR) without the need for 3D texture units or complex ray-casting algorithms [S1].
